    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. _extract_imports (java.py:816-849) never checks for '*': `import com.foo.client.*;` binds client -> com.foo.client. A call client.send() then gets dst_ref module com.foo.client and call_construct=function (java.py:2667, 3607-3626); the control `import com.foo.other.*;` gives external/method. _java_type_names says a type-import-on-demand binds nothing (java.py:1960-1961). r14, v05."  # 47e2
